        "original_id": "11349708-90af-5d71-bc96-513a40732401",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Minneapolis mayoral election, 2009; Minneapolis mayoral election, 2013\n- People: R. T. Rybak\n- Places: Minneapolis\n- Roles: Mayor of Minneapolis\n\nFacts:\n- R. T. Rybak took office as Mayor of Minneapolis in January 2002.\n- R. T. Rybak won a second term as Mayor of Minneapolis in November 2005.\n- The 2009 Minneapolis mayoral election was held on November 3, 2009 to elect the Mayor of Minneapolis for a four-year term.\n- R. T. Rybak won a third term in the 2009 Minneapolis mayoral election in the first round with 73.6% of the vote.\n- In late 2012, Mayor R. T. Rybak announced that he would not seek a fourth term.\n- After R. T. Rybak's late-2012 announcement, 35 candidates began campaigns in the 2013 Minneapolis mayoral election to replace him.",
